    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #354\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-235-system-i18n-01-05-add-stable-database-thr_49gc7rz8cw` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #235 ([system-i18n 01/05] Add stable database keys and nullable system names):\n\n- New migration `0027_database_keys_nullable_names.sql` adds a unique English camelCase `databases.key` column (mirroring `properties.key`), drops the `NOT NULL` constraint on `databases.name` and `properties.name`, and backfills `key`/nulls `name` for the ten hardcoded system databases (issue #24) on installs provisioned before this migration existed. Idempotent and additive per the expand/contract migration discipline.\n- `databasesStore.createDatabase` / `propertiesStore.createProperty` now require `name` only for non-system rows (application-level validation, not a DB constraint), and convert a duplicate `key` into a `ConflictError`.\n- `seedTenDatabases.ts` seeds the ten hardcoded databases and their built-in properties with a null `name` and their module id as `key`; view labels now source from the module-registry manifest instead of the now-nullable `database.name`.\n- `permissionManifest.ts` (the one in-repo consumer needing a display string) falls back to the raw `key` — not a translation — when `name` is null, per the issue's explicit scope until #147 wires a real i18n resolver.\n- New test file `databaseKeysNullableNames.test.ts` covers validation, duplicate-key rejection, the fresh-seed shape, and the pre-#235-schema migration upgrade path (including idempotency). `smoke.test.ts` updated for the new null-name reality.\n\nAll checks pass: full monorepo build, lint, format check, dependency-boundary check, and the complete test suite (114 unit + 716 integration + 5 e2e tests, 100% green).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
