    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #354\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed commit `987a2dc` to branch `bb/relay-235-system-i18n-01-05-add-stable-database-thr_49gc7rz8cw` (existing branch tied to PR #354, no new branch created).\n\nThis push fixes the HIGH-severity finding from the latest code review: the migration's `builtin_keys` allowlist for the `companies` database was missing `\"projects\"` — the key created by the `companies → projects` relate() call — which would have left that property's old English name un-nulled on an upgrade install while a fresh install always nulls it. Added a regression assertion covering `companies.projects` to the backfill test.\n\nVerified this turn: full build, lint, format check, `check:boundaries`, migration-numbering check, and all three test tiers (unit 114/114, integration 767/767, e2e 5/5) pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
